    "title": "Verb Periphrases",
    "subtitle": "auxiliary + infinitive, gerund or participle: volver a, soler, llevar + gerund, deber de, tener + participle and more",
    "footer": "Spanish Learning Program · B2 · Grammar · Verb periphrases",
    "next": "Next: B2 · PDF 5 — Infinitive, gerund and participle constructions"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "title": "After this PDF you can",
      "bullets": [
        "use verb periphrases with an infinitive (volver a, acabar de, dejar de, soler, ponerse a)",
        "use periphrases with a gerund (seguir, llevar, ir, andar, venir + gerund)",
        "use periphrases with a participle (tener, llevar, dar por + participle)",
        "choose between deber, deber de, tener que and haber que"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A <b>periphrasis</b> is a conjugated auxiliary verb plus an infinitive, gerund or participle. Only the first verb is conjugated; the second stays fixed. Pronouns can go before the auxiliary or after the infinitive / gerund: <i>Lo voy a hacer / Voy a hacerlo.</i>"
    },
    {
      "type": "h1",
      "text": "1. With an infinitive"
    },
    {
